{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Multiset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Multiset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.shell_iff_self_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.shell_iff_self_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L376-L383","doc":"Re-export 2: shell ↔ `λ` self-conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.shell_iff_kappa_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.shell_iff_kappa_zero","kind":"theorem","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L367-L374","doc":"Re-export 1: shell ↔ `κ_λ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.shell_iff_full_twist_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.shell_iff_full_twist_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L364-L364","doc":"The conjectural physical-to-algebraic equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L360-L360","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.toKappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.toKappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L360-L365","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.toFullTwistContentFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.toFullTwistContentFormula","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L360-L365","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture","kind":"class","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L344-L365","doc":"**Conjecture 1 — Categorical neutrality of saturated shells.**\n\nFor any `n`-strand saturated state with dominant Hecke label `λ`,\nthe following are equivalent at substrate `q`:\n\n* `λ` represents a stable completed shell.\n* The full twist `θ_n` acts trivially on `V_λ`.\n* `κ_λ = 0`.\n* `λ` is self-conjugate.\n\nThe first equivalence — between the *physical* shell predicate\nand the algebraic neutrality condition — is the conjectural\nframework claim. The remaining equivalences are derived from the\nHecke and partition-combinatorics typeclass fields. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.StableCompletedShell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.StableCompletedShell","kind":"def","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L333-L342","doc":"A **stable completed shell** is the (conjectural, framework-level)\nphysical predicate that `Φ_n` represents a global section of the\ncategorical mass endomorphism over the rigid braided monoidal\ncategory, with finite observable mass.\n\nConcrete model: defined as `isSelfConjugate λ`, the algebraic\navatar of shell completion (every box's content is matched by a\nnegation, so the multiset is balanced).  The genuine \"global\nsection with finite mass\" predicate is the upgrade target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_zero_iff_self_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_zero_iff_self_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L321-L329","doc":"Convenience iff packaging both directions: forward is the\nproved theorem, reverse is the typeclass field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.not_kappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.not_kappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L303-L319","doc":"**`KappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate` has no instance** (2026-11-15).\n`Saturated` is an empty `Prop` class, so `⟨⟩ : Saturated λ` exists for\nevery `λ`, and the field then claims every zero-sum content multiset is\nsymmetric. The abstract diagram with contents `{1, 2, -3}` refutes it.\n(A genuine Young diagram does too: `λ = (6,3,2,2,2)` has `κ = 0` and\nconjugate `(5,5,2,1,1,1)`.) So `SaturatedShellConjecture`, which extends\nthis class, is unsatisfiable as stated, and results conditional on it are\nvacuous until `Saturated` carries real content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.KappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate.kappa_zero_imp_self_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.KappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate.kappa_zero_imp_self_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L299-L299","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.KappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.KappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L298-L298","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.KappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.KappaZeroImpliesSelfConjugate","kind":"class","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L291-L301","doc":"**Partition arithmetic — reverse direction (axiomatised):** over\na *saturated* spectrum, `κ_λ = 0` *implies* self-conjugacy. The\nforward direction `isSelfConjugate λ → κ_λ = 0` is proved\nunconditionally as `kappa_zero_of_self_conjugate`; only the\nreverse implication needs Young-lattice structure (the saturation\nhypothesis pins a contents multiset with zero sum to a unique\nself-conjugate shape). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.FullTwistContentFormula.trivial_iff_kappa_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.FullTwistContentFormula.trivial_iff_kappa_zero","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L288-L288","doc":"The defining equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.FullTwistContentFormula.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.FullTwistContentFormula.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L286-L286","doc":"`q > 1` (substrate regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.FullTwistContentFormula.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.FullTwistContentFormula.mk","kind":"ctor","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L284-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.FullTwistContentFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.FullTwistContentFormula","kind":"class","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L278-L289","doc":"**Hecke folklore (axiomatised here)**: at generic `q > 1`, the\nfull twist acts trivially on `V_λ` iff `κ_λ = 0`.\n\nProvable in Mathas's framework once we wire up `H_n(q)`; the\naxiomatic exposure here keeps the present paper independent of\nthat future import. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.fullTwistTrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.fullTwistTrivial","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L264-L276","doc":"The full-twist eigenvalue. On `V_λ` the central element `θ_n`\nacts as the scalar `q^{2·κ_λ}`. The standard reference is\n[mathas1999, §3]; we expose the eigenvalue as an opaque map and\nrecord the equivalence \"trivial action ↔ κ = 0\" axiomatically.\n\n`fullTwistTrivial λ q` means that `θ_n` acts as the identity on\n`V_λ` at substrate parameter `q`.\n\nConcrete model: defined as `kappa λ = 0` (the algebraic\nconsequence of `θ_n = q^{2κ_λ} = 1` at generic q).  The genuine\nHecke-algebra reading awaits the `H_n(q)` import. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.Saturated.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.Saturated.mk","kind":"ctor","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L260-L260","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.Saturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.Saturated","kind":"class","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L245-L260","doc":"A **saturated spectrum** is one in which every box of `λ`\ncontributes its content exactly once with no external\nweighting. The locality-free reading of the categorical mass\nendomorphism `Φ_n` is built into `Saturated`: if a state is\nsaturated, the brane-tower contribution is governed entirely by\nthe multiset `λ.contents`. Concrete instances expose `λ` as the\ndominant irreducible label of the Hecke module `V_λ`.\n\n`@marker` — intentional opaque structural predicate. The full\nsaturation condition is a statement about the Young-lattice\nstructure of `λ` and awaits the `H_n(q)` Hecke-algebra import\n(exactly as `fullTwistTrivial` below does); until then it is a\ndeliberate empty-`Prop` tag, not an accidental vacuous carrier.\nIt is a *hypothesis* gate on the reverse implication\n`κ_λ = 0 → self-conjugate`, never discharged by an instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_singletonDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_singletonDiagram","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L210-L213","doc":"Charge of a singleton diagram is its content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.singletonDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.singletonDiagram","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L203-L208","doc":"The single-box Young diagram with content `c`. Used as the base\ncase for inductive arguments on shape complexity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.unionDiagram_isSelfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.unionDiagram_isSelfConjugate","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L176-L199","doc":"**Self-conjugacy is preserved under disjoint union.** If both\n`λ` and `μ` are self-conjugate, so is `unionDiagram λ μ`. Pure\nMultiset arithmetic — `Multiset.map_add` plus the constituent\nself-conjugacies' contents equalities. No axioms.\n\nThis is the abstract analogue of the LR-rigidity claim for the\ntrivial union composite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_unionDiagram_empty_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_unionDiagram_empty_right","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L172-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_unionDiagram_empty_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_unionDiagram_empty_left","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L166-L170","doc":"The empty diagram is a left/right identity for `unionDiagram` at\nthe level of contents and charge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_unionDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_unionDiagram","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L156-L164","doc":"**Additivity of Jucys–Murphy charge.** Charge is linear over\nmultiset disjoint union: `κ(λ ⊔ μ) = κ(λ) + κ(μ)`. This is the\nabstract version of the LR content-additivity claim used in\n`LRFusion.ContentAdditive`. Provable directly from\n`Multiset.sum_add`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.unionDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.unionDiagram","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L147-L154","doc":"Disjoint union of two Young diagrams (multiset union of their\ncontents). The corresponding combinatorial operation is\n\"horizontal concatenation\" of partition contents — useful when\nsplitting a composite analysis along constituent shells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.emptyDiagram_isSelfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.emptyDiagram_isSelfConjugate","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L135-L143","doc":"The empty diagram is self-conjugate (negating the empty multiset\ngives the empty multiset). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_emptyDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_emptyDiagram","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L131-L133","doc":"The empty diagram has zero charge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.emptyDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.emptyDiagram","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L123-L129","doc":"**Empty Young diagram** (the unique `n = 0` shape): no boxes, no\ncontents, charge zero, self-conjugate. Smoke-test instance for\nthe framework. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_zero_of_self_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_zero_of_self_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L109-L121","doc":"**Forward direction (provable):** a self-conjugate diagram has\nzero global Jucys–Murphy charge. Proof: `κ_λ = κ_{λ'} = -κ_λ`,\nso `2 κ_λ = 0`, hence `κ_λ = 0` over `ℤ`. This is pure\nmultiset arithmetic — no Hecke / Young-lattice structure needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.conjugate_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.conjugate_involution","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L95-L107","doc":"**Conjugation is an involution.** `(λ')' = λ`: negating contents\ntwice is the identity on the multiset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L81-L93","doc":"`κ_{λ'} = -κ_λ`. The contents multiset of the conjugate diagram\nis obtained by negating each entry, so its sum negates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.isSelfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.isSelfConjugate","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L77-L79","doc":"A diagram is **self-conjugate** when it equals its conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.conjugate","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L70-L75","doc":"Conjugate (transposed) Young diagram: contents flip sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.kappa","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L67-L68","doc":"Total Jucys–Murphy charge `κ_λ := Σ_{x ∈ λ} c(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram.card_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram.card_eq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The multiset has exactly `n` boxes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram.contents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram.contents","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Multiset of Jucys–Murphy contents `{c(x) : x ∈ λ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram.n","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Number of strands `n = |λ|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality.YoungDiagram","kind":"structure","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellNeutrality.lean#L55-L65","doc":"A Young diagram, encoded by the box-set of its underlying\npartition. The Jucys–Murphy content of a box `(i, j)` is the\ninteger `j - i`; we treat the diagram abstractly via its content\nmultiset. ","signatureChunk":0}]}